## B4b/B4c limits

The intermediate no-testable abort is intentionally retained. Rejection-only lifecycle completion is not implemented or claimed. B4b must add valid no-testable record publication/checkpoint/cleanup without a critic; exact finalized-round candidate/role authority for mixed and rejection-only records; and resume behavior without duplicate provider work or deadline extension. `_verify_finalized_discovery_rounds` retains its rendered-only IDs and mandatory three-role tuple. `_completed_result` itself has no direct critic check; audit it with its callers rather than assuming one. Existing completion, recovery, cleanup, summaries and role budgeting were not edited.

B4c must retain invalid hypotheses in history/novelty and provide bounded closed numeric rejection feedback to the next investigator. Two rejection-only lifecycle rounds do not count as two evaluated feedback rounds. Current campaign budgets/readiness still prohibit a new campaign from this checkpoint.

No tests were read, created, changed or run. No synthetic probes, events, references, records or responses were fabricated. No model/API calls, credentials, candidate evaluation, campaign launch/resume/poll, evaluator rebuild, commits, pushes or deployment occurred. All older review packages and archived artifacts were preserved.
